## Latest Reported Global EV Sales Figures for 2026

The most recent reported data covers sales through June 2026. Global electric vehicle sales reached approximately **2.0 million units in June 2026**, bringing the cumulative total for the first half of the year to roughly **9.6 million units**, according to Benchmark Mineral Intelligence. [1](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [2](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [4](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [5](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)

### Growth Rates

June 2026 sales increased by about **7% year-over-year** and **11% month-over-month**, reflecting improving demand across several major markets. [1](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [2](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)

### Regional Breakdown

- **Europe:** The standout growth leader in 2026. Registrations jumped **31% year-over-year** in June and **28% month-over-month**, pushing the year-to-date total **27% higher** than the first half of 2025. Several markets including France, Denmark, Spain, and Portugal recorded their highest-ever monthly EV sales. [1](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [2](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [5](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)
- **China:** Remains the world's largest single market with roughly **1.0 million units sold in June**, but the domestic market has softened considerably. Sales fell **11% year-over-year** in June and are down **14% year-to-date** compared with the same period in 2025. Chinese manufacturers are increasingly offsetting weaker domestic demand by expanding exports. [2](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [5](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)
- **North America:** Lagging behind other regions, with EV sales down **20% year-to-date** in 2026. Weaker policy support and the upcoming expiration of the U.S. federal EV tax credit have contributed to slower adoption, and several legacy automakers have slowed their electrification plans. [1](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [2](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [5](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)
- **Rest of World:** Emerging markets are showing the fastest relative growth, with sales surging **98% year-over-year** to reach **1.4 million units year-to-date**. [2](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP) [5](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)

### Brand Performance (January–May 2026)

Among individual manufacturers, **BYD** led global EV sales in the first five months of 2026 with **1,249,405 units sold**, more than double **Tesla's 595,647 units** over the same period. BYD continues to thrive overseas even as its domestic sales face pressure. [8](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)

### Full-Year Context

Comprehensive full-year data for calendar year 2026 has not yet been finalized. For historical context, global EV sales exceeded **20 million units in 2025**. The International Energy Agency's *Global EV Outlook 2026* forecasts approximately **23 million global EV sales** for the full year. [6](#ORXWNIwytbseQ2uP)

